  "problem_statement": "strip_scheme function raises UnboundLocalError when processing URLs\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `strip_scheme()` function in furl.py is raising an `UnboundLocalError` when trying to process URLs. The error occurs because a local variable `scheme` is being referenced before assignment.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport furl\n\n# This will raise UnboundLocalError\nf = furl.furl('http://www.example.com/')\nprint(f.url)\n```\n\nThe error also occurs with various URL manipulations:\n\n```python\nimport furl\n\nf = furl.furl('http://www.pumps.com/')\nf.args.setdefault('foo', 'blah')  # UnboundLocalError\n```\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nThe URL should be parsed and manipulated correctly without raising an UnboundLocalError.\n\n#### Actual Behavior\n\n```\nUnboundLocalError: local variable 'scheme' referenced before assignment\n```\n\nThis affects basic URL creation and manipulation operations throughout the furl library."
}